        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T18:38:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, yes, this is a difference in C and C++ I believe. It\u0027s considered variable-length in C, but not C++.\n\nIt looks like there is a \"-Wvla\" flag and it seems to work (see below), so we should enable it (at least on the fpsensor files) to remove any ambiguity and prevent issues in the future.\n\n\n make V\u003d1 run-fpsensor\n\n test/fpsensor.c: In function ‘test_vla’:\ntest/fpsensor.c:319:2: error: variable length array ‘arr’ is used [-Werror\u003dvla]\n  int arr[array_size()];\n\n\n diff --git a/Makefile.toolchain b/Makefile.toolchain\nindex 49a453d1a..c90fa9ba7 100644\n--- a/Makefile.toolchain\n+++ b/Makefile.toolchain\n@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ PROTOC?\u003dprotoc\n C_WARN \u003d -Wstrict-prototypes -Wdeclaration-after-statement -Wno-pointer-sign\n COMMON_WARN \u003d -Wall -Wundef -Werror -Werror-implicit-function-declaration \\\n        -Wno-trigraphs -Wno-format-security -Wno-address-of-packed-member \\\n-       -fno-common -fno-strict-aliasing -fno-strict-overflow\n+       -fno-common -fno-strict-aliasing -fno-strict-overflow -Wvla\n \n UBSAN_FLAGS\u003d-fsanitize\u003darray-bounds,vla-bound \\\n        -fno-sanitize\u003dvptr \\\ndiff --git a/test/fpsensor.c b/test/fpsensor.c\nindex 33998b6b0..1c91222c8 100644\n--- a/test/fpsensor.c\n+++ b/test/fpsensor.c\n@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@\n  * found in the LICENSE file.\n  */\n \n+#include \u003cstdlib.h\u003e\n #include \"common.h\"\n #include \"ec_commands.h\"\n #include \"fpsensor_crypto.h\"\n@@ -310,8 +311,21 @@ test_static int test_fp_set_sensor_mode(void)\n        return EC_SUCCESS;\n }\n \n+static int array_size(void) {\n+       return rand() % 10;\n+}\n+\n+test_static int test_vla(void) {\n+       int arr[array_size()];\n+       arr[0] \u003d 1;\n+       TEST_ASSERT(arr[0] \u003d\u003d 1);\n+       TEST_ASSERT(1);\n+       return EC_SUCCESS;\n+}\n+\n void run_test(void)\n {\n+       RUN_TEST(test_vla);\n        RUN_TEST(test_fp_enc_status_valid_flags);\n        RUN_TEST(test_fp_tpm_seed_not_set);\n        RUN_TEST(test_derive_encryption_key_failure_seed_not_set);",
      "parentUuid": "6dbc030e_62c644b9",
